      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301276",
      ":question/problem": "A large orchard covers $180$ acres. To estimate the total number of apple trees, an agricultural researcher randomly selects $6$ different $1$-acre plots and counts the trees in each plot. The numbers of trees in these plots are $42$, $57$, $49$, $61$, $54$, and $46$.\n\nBased on the **mean** of the sample, which of the following ranges contains the best estimate for the number of trees in the entire orchard?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
