      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301277",
      ":question/problem": "A sports analyst wants to estimate the typical number of points scored by a local basketball team in a season. The team has played in $320$ games over the past several years. The analyst randomly selects $7$ of those games and records the points scored: $102$, $96$, $88$, $105$, $99$, $94$, and $110$.\n\nBased on the **median** of the sample, which of the following ranges contains the best estimate for the total number of points scored in all $320$ games?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
